bsp-registry-tools (2.2.2-2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Provide /usr/bin/kas-container as a symlink to the bundled venv copy
    so "bsp build" finds it on PATH (previously only bsp-kas-container
    was exposed).
  * Pin the bundled kas to KAS_VERSION (default 5.5, overridable at
    build time) so kas-container matches the registry container
    definitions.
  * Fail the build (debian/check-kas-container) if the staged package
    lacks an executable kas-container or its --version does not match
    KAS_VERSION.
  * Move "docker.io | podman" from Recommends to Depends: kas-container
    requires a container runtime.
  * Add an autopkgtest verifying kas-container is on PATH and runs.

 -- Mikhail Tsukerman <mikhail.tsukerman@advantech.com>  Thu, 30 Oct 2025 14:00:00 +0000

bsp-registry-tools (2.2.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial Debian package built with dh-virtualenv: all Python
    dependencies (server, gui, mcp, completions and deploy extras,
    including kas) are bundled in /opt/venvs/bsp-registry-tools.
  * Expose bsp, bsp-explorer, bsp-explorer-web and bsp-mcp via
    /usr/bin symlinks; the bundled kas is exposed as /usr/bin/bsp-kas.
  * Ship systemd units for the REST/GraphQL server, the MCP server and
    the web explorer (disabled by default).
  * Install a static bash completion script for bsp and the registry
    examples under /usr/share/bsp-registry-tools/examples.

 -- Mikhail Tsukerman <mikhail.tsukerman@advantech.com>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 20:00:00 +0000
